==German==
{{wikipedia|dab=Hahn|lang=de}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|hano}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*hanô}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*kan-||to sing}}. Compare Dutch {{m|nl|haan}}, Danish {{m|da|hane}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/haːn/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-Hahn.OGG|audio|lang=de}}
* {{rhymes|aːn|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m|Hahns|gen2=Hahnes|Hähne|pl2=Hahnen|Hähnchen|dim2=Hähnlein}}

# [[cock]], [[rooster]]
# [[stopcock]], [[tap]], [[spigot]], [[faucet]]

====Declension====
{{de-decl-noun-m|(e)s|pl=Hähne}}

====Usage notes====
* The normal plural is '''''Hähne'''''.
* The plural ''Hahnen'' is obsolete or dialectal (the last remnant of what was once a weak noun).

===Proper noun===
{{de-proper noun|m|g2=f}}

# {{surname|common|from=nicknames|lang=de|dot=}} originating as a nickname.

